tainable=False in the insufficiency-only block but does not address the pop path guarding on _is_no_verdict_fault"],"finding":"Fix B must survive reconcile_verdict's own second-pass marker clearing: the in-file `_is_no_verdict_fault` guard (line 71) plus the `result.pop('verdict_obtainable', None)` at line 189 will strip the marker on a second reconcile pass for an insufficiency-only FAIL, because such a verdict has real criteria findings and does NOT match `_is_no_verdict_fault` (which requires exactly one finding named NO_VERDICT_CRITERION).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4cb71f3a4255ab37","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py:71-82 (`_is_no_verdict_fault`), :181-189 (second-pass pop); Plan Fix B","norm_id":"n951a672753001c64","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Sidecar path re-runs reconcile_verdict over an in-place-mutated copy; an insufficiency-only FAIL's verdict_obtainable=False is popped on the second pass and the durable/close disposition reverts to exit 1"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have Fix B either derive `verdict_obtainable` idempotently inside the insufficiency-only block on every pass, or extend the line-181 guard so an insufficiency-only FAIL is recognized as an already-reconciled retryable disposition and not popped.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_