nd NOT on the bank entry's evidence-string `truncated=True` flag (which can mark a genuine refutation), so genuine met=false-with-evidence still blocks (AC line 2).","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Fix A: 'a criterion with NO conclusive bank entry (un-evaluated / truncated) is stamped evidence_sufficient=False'","Plan impacted-sites: 'un-banked met=false -> insufficiency, guarded on truncation/no-conclusive-entry'","completion_banking.py:474-482 upsert: 'truncated = len(text) > EVIDENCE_CAP_CHARS ... a capped entry carries an explicit truncated=True flag' — string capping, not verifier-run truncation","completion_verdict_assembly.py:52 _entry_actionable_block: met is False and not _entry_insufficient — a truncated-evidence met=false with no marker is still a GENUINE banked refutation","AC line 2 requires genuine met=false-with-conclusive-evidence to still block exit 1 (non-masking)"],"finding":"Fix A's insufficiency-reclassification decision rule is ambiguously specified: it names both 'un-banked' (entry is None) and 'truncation' as triggers, but 'truncated' is an existing bank-entry flag meaning evidence-string capping (3000 chars) - and a truncated-evidence met=false entry with no evidence_sufficient marker is a GENUINE refutation, so keying reclassification on it would mask real failures.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc222ea65dee2828f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Fix A; Impacted sites (completion_verdict_assembly.py note 'guarded on truncation/no-conclusive-entry')","norm_id":"n633259a7ae05e148","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion was genuinely evaluated and refuted (met=false, no insufficiency marker) but its evidence string exceeded 3000 chars so entry.truncated=True; if Fix A keys on the truncated flag it is reclassified as insufficiency and the ticket wrongly takes the retryable 